        "text": "Therefore, tokens can be categorized into different types according to their function and purpose. For example, transactional tokens serve as units of account and are used to exchange goods and services. Governance tokens give token holders the right to vote on governance issues of a protocol. Utility tokens are used as a form of payment within a specific ecosystem. There are also security tokens, equity tokens, liquidity provider tokens, and new types of tokens are likely to be created in the future as the crypto industry continues to innovate. When it comes to tokens, you can also mint millions of identical ones or mint a select few with unique properties. You've probably heard about non Fungible tokens, or NFTs. NFTs are cryptographic assets on a blockchain with unique identification codes and metadata that distinguish each token from another. Non fungible means items are not interchangeable because each has unique properties.",
